    {
      "id": "mechanism",
      "text": "Under the rotor sits the swashplate: one plate stays still, one spins. Pull the collective lever, and the whole plate rises. Every blade bites harder, so it climbs. Push the cyclic stick, and the plate tilts. Each blade bites harder on one side, the rotor tilts, and the helicopter goes that way.",
